{
  "about": [
    "What the steady-noise check (SpeechGate.isSteady on the Mac, isSteady in desktop/src/core/speech.ts) must call steady and what it must keep.",
    "Read by Tests/SatzKitTests/CodexFixSteadyNoiseTests.swift and desktop/test/codexFixSteadyNoise.test.ts, so both platforms answer every case the same way.",
    "Each case is `seconds` of 16 kHz audio: `noise` (none is digital silence), plus ja-genau.wav (\"Ja, genau.\", 0.83 s) added at `clip.at` seconds, times `clip.gain` (1 if absent).",
    "white: x = (1664525 x + 1013904223) mod 2^32 from x = seed, each sample x / 2^32 * 2 - 1 (Codex's generator, so the first two cases are its F01 fixtures).",
    "hiss: white times amplitude. fan: white through low = 0.92 low + white, scaled to an RMS of level. tone: amplitude sin(2 pi hertz i / 16000).",
    "fan with `pole` 0.99 instead of 0.92 is rumble. pink: white through Paul Kellet's filter (b0..b6 below in both tests), scaled to an RMS of level. `taps`: at each second given, a key thump 0.12 exp(-i/100) (sin(2 pi 180 i/16000) + 0.5 sin(2 pi 2200 i/16000)) for 400 samples. `clip.until`: only the clip's first seconds (0.36 is \"Ja,\")."
  ],
